NAME
       ssh-agent - keep unlocked private keys in memory for ssh

SYNOPSIS
       ssh-agent [-k]
       eval $(ssh-agent)

DESCRIPTION
       ssh-agent is a small background program that holds private keys after
       their passphrase was typed once (with ssh-add). ssh, scp and
       ssh-copy-id ask the agent to sign logins, so you are not asked for the
       passphrase again during the session.

       When it starts, ssh-agent prints shell commands that set
       SSH_AUTH_SOCK and SSH_AGENT_PID. Run it inside eval so that your shell
       runs those commands; otherwise ssh-add cannot find the agent.

OPTIONS
       -k     Stop the agent named by SSH_AGENT_PID.

EXAMPLES
           eval $(ssh-agent)
           ssh-add

SEE ALSO
       ssh-add(1), ssh(1), ssh-keygen(1)
